#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# depth

#% text
# `depth(t)` gives 1 for an atom and one more than the depth of its deepest argument for a compound term.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
depth(x)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
depth(f(x))
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
depth([1, [2, [3]]])
#% output
#= 4

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Heads do not count:

#% cell
depth(f(a)(b))
#% output
#= 2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `leaf_count`, `array_depth`, `level`
